{"id":952,"slug":"tanner-88","title":"Tanner ’88","year":1988,"country":"United States","duration":353,"spine":258,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/952-tanner-88","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/737b414279e7a0df660ac086e87c64ae/kEmt8wcBIShHoV7oEBzALnZY2uYuim_large.jpg","description":"In 1988, renegade filmmaker Robert Altman and Pulitzer Prize–winning Doonesbury cartoonist Garry Trudeau created a presidential candidate, ran him alongside the other hopefuls during the primary season, and presented their media campaign as a cross between a soap opera and TV news. The result was the groundbreaking Tanner ’88, a piercing satire of media-age American politics, in which actors Michael Murphy (as  contender Jack Tanner) and  Cynthia Nixon (as his daughter) rub elbows on the campaign trail with real-life political players Jesse Jackson, Gary Hart, Bob Dole, Ralph Nader, Kitty Dukakis, and Gloria Steinem, among many others. The Criterion Collection is proud to present the complete eleven-episode television series—more relevant today than ever. ","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Robert Altman","slug":"robert-altman"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Michael Murphy","role":"Jack Tanner","slug":"michael-murphy"},{"actor":"Pamela Reed","role":"TJ Cavanaugh","slug":"pamela-reed"},{"actor":"Cynthia Nixon","role":"Alex Tanner","slug":"cynthia-nixon"},{"actor":"Kevin J. O’Connor","role":"Hayes Haggerty","slug":"kevin-j-oconnor"},{"actor":"Daniel Jenkins","role":"Stringer Kincaid","slug":"daniel-jenkins"},{"actor":"Jim Fyfe","role":"Emile Berkoff","slug":"jim-fyfe"},{"actor":"Matt Malloy","role":"Deke Connors","slug":"matt-malloy"},{"actor":"Ilana Levine","role":"Andrea Spinelli","slug":"ilana-levine"},{"actor":"Richard Cox","role":"David Seidelman","slug":"richard-cox"},{"actor":"Veronica Cartwright","role":"Molly Hark","slug":"veronica-cartwright"},{"actor":"Sandra Bowie","role":"Stevie Chevalier","slug":"sandra-bowie"},{"actor":"Wendy Crewson","rol